      "writtenOn": "2026-03-27T21:15:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just an observation that the `MutexCondVarProtected` API feels a bit odd to me. Why should the caller have to call `Use()` on it to just `Wait(For)`? Why can\u0027t `Wait(For)` be methods on the `MutexCondVarProtected` instead of the `CondVarGuard` which probably shouldn\u0027t exist in the first place. I.e. there should be a `Use()` method on the `MutexCondVarProtected` but it should just return a mutex `Guard` instead of `CondVarGuard`.\n\nAnd finally, the predicate should ideally get a const ref to the state so that it can\u0027t mutate it, right? WDYT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 125,
        "endChar": 96
      },
